# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT — iBless

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer and application architect.

Your task is to design and build a complete, functional, responsive web application called **iBless**.

Do not merely produce a design prototype, static mock-up or frontend demonstration. Build an actual working application with real authentication, persistent data storage, multi-user interactions and functional features.

You are responsible for:
- Designing the application.
- Establishing the technical architecture.
- Implementing the frontend.
- Implementing Firebase integration.
- Designing and implementing the database structure.
- Implementing authentication and access controls.
- Implementing all core user journeys.
- Testing the application.
- Providing clear setup and deployment instructions.

Work autonomously wherever requirements are sufficiently defined. Make sensible implementation decisions rather than repeatedly asking for clarification.

If a Firebase configuration or other external credential is required, create the necessary configuration structure and clearly document what I need to supply. Never invent credentials or claim that an external service has been connected when it has not.

