# 17. FIREBASE SECURITY

Security is important even though this is a personal joke application.

Implement actual Firestore security rules.

Requirements:

- Authenticated users only for private application functionality.
- Users can update only their own profiles.
- Users can read only blessings they are entitled to access.
- Public blessings are readable by authenticated users.
- Private blessings are accessible only to their sender and recipient.
- Only authorised users can modify blessing status.
- Only relevant participants can access private requests.
- Users cannot impersonate other users.
- Users cannot access private notifications belonging to other accounts.
- Users cannot arbitrarily manipulate other users' statistics.

Implement appropriate Firebase Storage rules for profile pictures.

Never expose private credentials or service-account keys in frontend code.

Firebase's public web configuration may be supplied through the normal application configuration process; actual access control must come from security rules and authentication.

Provide clear instructions for deploying security rules.

Do not claim the application is secure without implementing and testing the rules.

